T48 local patch: 8049 pin phases on both XTAL1 edges, first cycle at S1.

Upstream base: github.com/devsaurus/t48 commit 837bd24, rtl/vhdl, copied
unchanged to rtl/t48/vhdl.  make refresh-t48-netlist copies rtl/t48/vhdl,
applies this patch (patch -p1) and builds rtl/t48/t48_core_synth.v.

Changes (MCS-48 data sheet A.C. table, User's Manual cycle timing; the
simulator's sim/chips/cpu8049 phases):
- t48_core, t48_clock_ctrl: new input xtal_fall_en_i, the XTAL1 fall
  enable, beside xtal_en_i (the rise).
- ALE: rises at the start of S4 (as upstream), falls on the XTAL1 fall
  after the end of S4: 3.5 periods (tLL; upstream 2).
- RD-, WR-: fall on the XTAL1 fall after the start of S1 of the second
  machine cycle, 3 periods after ALE falls (tLAFC1; upstream at the end of
  XTAL2 of S5 of the first cycle), rise at the end of XTAL2 of S3 of the
  second cycle, 7.5 periods Low (tCC1; upstream at the end of S2).  The
  request is held from the end of S5 to that fall and dropped at the next
  XTAL1 rise or a state resync.
- RESET: the clock state machine resets to the end of S5 (xtal_q = 2,
  MSTATE5) so the first XTAL1 rise after RESET opens S1 of the instruction
  at address 0 (upstream: MSTATE3 of a virtual NOP, ALE 3 periods after
  the release).  INFERRED: the data sheet does not give the first state
  after RESET; this follows the User's Manual reading of the simulator.
- P2: the port latch drives the pins directly, so a P2 write shows in the
  state it is made in, as on P1 (upstream one XTAL1 period later through
  an XTAL-clocked output register; PCH keeps it).
  For MOVD/ANLD/ORLD this leaves the P2 nibble no hold after the PROG-
  fall (upstream 1t); there is no 8243 on the WD1003-CMD.
- PSEN-, PROG- unchanged (they do not move with EA Low and no 8243).

